<section id="S7" class="ltx_section">
<h2 class="ltx_title ltx_title_section"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_section">VII </span><span id="S7.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Conclusion</span></h2>

<div id="S7.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S7.p1.1" class="ltx_p">In this paper, we propose <span id="S7.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">DyQ-VLA</span>, a dynamic quantization framework for real-time Vision-Language-Action (VLA) edge deployment.
By leveraging a sensitivity-aware switching strategy based on kinematic metrics, <span id="S7.p1.1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">DyQ-VLA</span> effectively monitors temporal-dynamic quantization sensitivity.
Furthermore, we propose a kinematic-guided bit allocation module to assign optimal bit-widths for manipulation accuracy.
Experiments validate <span id="S7.p1.1.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">DyQ-VLA</span>’s efficient performance, achieving speedups of <math id="S7.p1.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="1.49\times" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>1.49</mn><mo lspace="0.222em">×</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">1.49\times</annotation></semantics></math> in simulation and up to <math id="S7.p1.m2" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="1.43\times" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>1.43</mn><mo lspace="0.222em">×</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">1.43\times</annotation></semantics></math> in the real world.
Notably, it requires only 30.9% of the memory footprint while maintaining 99.5% performance, establishing a novel paradigm for real-time edge deployment.</p>
</div>
</section>
